.\" $GergiOS$
.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt CAPSH 1
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm capsh
.Nd view and modify process capabilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -get
.Nm
.Fl -bound
.Nm
.Fl -set Ns = Ns Ar cap_list
.Nm
.Fl -decode Ns = Ns Ar hex
.Nm
.Fl -list
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility displays and modifies the capability sets of the calling process.
.Pp
Capabilities are named privileges that control access to sensitive
operations (I/O ports, IRQ allocation, filesystem mount, etc.).
See
.Xr capabilities 7
for a complete list.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width "-set=cap_list"
.It Fl -get
Display the effective capability set of the current process as a hex
mask and a list of capability names.
.It Fl -bound
Display the bounding set (the immutable upper limit on capabilities
that may ever be granted to this process).
.It Fl -set Ns = Ns Ar cap_list
Set the effective capability set to the specified capabilities.
.Ar cap_list
is a comma-separated list of capability names
(e.g.,
.Li IPC_OWNER,NET_BIND )
or a hex mask
(e.g.,
.Li 0x44 ) .
.It Fl -decode Ns = Ns Ar hex
Decode a hex capability mask into human-readable capability names
without modifying any process state.
.It Fl -list
List all known capabilities with their names, bit positions, and masks,
as well as the predefined capability sets
.Pq CAP_BASE , CAP_SYSTEM , CAP_DRIVER , CAP_NETWORK , CAP_ADMIN , CAP_FULL .
.It Fl -help
Print a usage message and exit.
.El
.Pp
Only one of
.Fl -get ,
.Fl -bound ,
.Fl -set ,
.Fl -decode ,
or
.Fl -list
may be specified at a time.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ capsh --get
effective    0x0044  (IPC_OWNER,NET_BIND)

$ capsh --bound
bounding     0x1fff  (SYS_RAWIO,NET_RAW,NET_BIND,NET_ADMIN,SYS_ADMIN,...)

$ capsh --set=IPC_OWNER,NET_BIND
capabilities set: 0x0044

$ capsh --decode=0x1fff
decode       0x1fff  (SYS_RAWIO,NET_RAW,NET_BIND,NET_ADMIN,SYS_ADMIN,...)

$ capsh --list
Known capabilities (13 total):
  Name                  Bit    Mask
  ----                  ---    ----
  SYS_RAWIO             bit 0  0x0001
  NET_RAW               bit 1  0x0002
  ...
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_get_proc 2 ,
.Xr cap_set_proc 2 ,
.Xr cap_get_bound 2 ,
.Xr capabilities 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in GergiOS.
